      "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn Quot, Theorem <REF_0001>\nthe assumption that <MATH_0001> is flat is not necessary.\nIn this section we modify the method of proof based on ideas from\nderived algebraic geometry to get around the flatness hypothesis.\nAn entirely different method is used in\nQuot, Section <REF_0002>\nto get exactly the same result; this is why the\nmethod from this section is obsolete.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThe only step in the proof of\nQuot, Theorem <REF_0003>\nwhich uses flatness is in the application of\nQuot, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nThe lemma is used to construct an obstruction theory as in\nArtin's Axioms, Section <REF_0005>.\nThe proof of the lemma relies on\nDeformation Theory, Lemmas <REF_0006> and\n<REF_0007> from\nDeformation Theory, Section <REF_0008>.\nThis is how the assumption that <MATH_0002> is flat comes about.\nBefore we go on, note that results (2) and (3) of\nDeformation Theory, Lemmas <REF_0009>\ndo hold without the assumption that <MATH_0003> is flat as they rely\non Deformation Theory, Lemmas <REF_0010>\nand <REF_0011>\nwhich do not have any flatness assumptions.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nBefore we give the details we give some motivation for the construction\nfrom derived algebraic geometry, since we think it will clarify what\nfollows. Let <MATH_0004> be a finite type algebra over the locally Noetherian\nbase <MATH_0005>. Denote <MATH_0006> a ``derived base change''\nof <MATH_0007> to <MATH_0008> and denote <MATH_0009> the\ncanonical inclusion morphism. The object <MATH_0010>\ndoes not (yet) have a definition in the Stacks project; we may think of it\nas the algebraic space <MATH_0011> endowed with a simplicial sheaf of rings\n<MATH_0012> whose homology sheaves are\n<MATH_0013>\nThe morphism <MATH_0014> is flat\n(the terms of the simplicial sheaf of rings being <MATH_0015>-flat),\nso the usual material for deformations of flat modules applies to it.\nThus we see that we get an obstruction theory using the groups\n<MATH_0016>\nwhere <MATH_0017> for inf auts, inf defs, obstructions. Note that\na flat deformation of <MATH_0018> to <MATH_0019>\nis automatically of the form <MATH_0020> where <MATH_0021>\nis a flat deformation of <MATH_0022>. By adjunction\nof the functors <MATH_0023> and <MATH_0024> these ext groups are equal to\n<MATH_0025>\nThus we obtain obstruction groups of exactly the same form as in the\nproof of Quot, Lemma <REF_0012>\nwith the only change being\nthat one replaces the first occurrence of <MATH_0026> by the complex\n<MATH_0027>.\n\n<STRUCT_0006><STRUCT_0007>\nBelow we prove the non-flat version of the lemma by a ``direct''\nconstruction of <MATH_0028> and direct\nproof of its relationship to the deformation theory of <MATH_0029>.\nIn fact, it suffices to construct <MATH_0030>, as we\nare only interested in the ext groups\n<MATH_0031>\nfor <MATH_0032>. We can even identify the cohomology sheaves\n<MATHSEG_0001>if <MATHSEG_0002>if <MATHSEG_0003>if <MATHSEG_0004>if <MATHSEG_0005>\nThis observation will guide our construction of <MATH_0033>\nin the remarks below.\n\n",
